Z||000000||mrfixit58||05-11-2001||09:21 PM||||I'm trying to use PIP to add a picture to my signature. This is what I have in profile:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip[/IMG]" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip[/IMG]</A> <P>What wrong?<P>Roy<P>------------------<BR>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip">   <P>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 05-11-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 05-11-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||05-12-2001||01:50 AM||||You need to put [IMG] in front of that. Should work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||05-12-2001||03:23 AM||||Launch your PIP program.<P>Click on the HISTORY button.<P>Click on the image you want.<P>Press CTRL V<P>Then go into the POST here on the forum and press CTRL V again (or into your profile page and do the same for Signature).  It will paste the code with the necesary IMG tags.<P>Noticed, you don't have the correct link to your photo.<P>It should look like this (the IMG tags removed for display purposes.<P>Copy this and just put your photo name where jsocha.jpg is currently located.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg</A>  <P>along with the respective IMG tags and you should have it<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
